# shellcheck configuration for the FERAL MULE repository.
#
# Rules are adjusted deliberately and with a reason, never disabled wholesale.
# See CONTRIBUTING.md: "If a linter cannot pass on something, adjust the rule
# deliberately in its config with a comment explaining why."

# SC2016: "Expressions don't expand in single quotes, use double quotes."
#
# Disabled repository-wide, for one specific reason. The generators in tools/
# emit Markdown, and Markdown uses backticks for inline code. Every generated
# line such as
#
#     printf 'See `docs/adr/README.md`.\n'
#
# trips SC2016, because shellcheck reads the backticks as an unexpanded
# command substitution. They are literal output. Single quotes are the CORRECT
# choice here: switching to double quotes would make the shell attempt the
# substitution, which is the bug SC2016 exists to warn about.
#
# Roughly twenty such lines exist across gen-status.sh, gen-traceability.sh and
# new-trade.sh. Annotating each individually would add more noise than the rule
# removes, and would not be maintained.
#
# The trade-off accepted: a genuine missing expansion inside a single-quoted
# printf will not be caught by shellcheck. Every generator writes to a checked
# output (gen-status.sh --check, gen-traceability.sh --check), so an
# unexpanded variable appears as a literal in a file CI compares.
disable=SC2016
